parseutf8csv=:3 : 0

NB.*parseutf8csv  v-- parses excel  comma delimited BOM  prefixed
NB. utf8 csv.
NB.
NB. This verb cuts apart the csv utf8 version of my LLSGS theorem
NB. candidate spreadsheet. I  wanted a  form  that  is more  diff
NB. friendly and easiar to hack when building LaTeX documents.
NB.
NB. monad:  btcl =. parseutf8csv clCsv
NB.
NB.   NB. read sheet saved as CSV UTF8
NB.   csv=. utf8 read jpath '~LEAN/sheets/theorem_candidates.csv'
NB.   txt=. parseutf8csv csv

NB. strip byte order
bw=. #BOM
c=. (bw * BOM -: bw {. y) }. y

NB. form table of sheet rows
c=. ',' ,. allwhitetrim&> (CRLF E. c) <;.2 c

NB. bit mask of unquoted " field delimiters
b=. -. }. ~:/\ '"' e.~  ' ' , ,c
b=. ($c) $ b *. , ',' = c

NB. form ct in each cell
c=. ];._2&.> tlf&.> b <;._1"1 c

NB. replace "s and justify
c=. ljust@('" '&charsub)&.> c

NB. format particular columns
hdr=. allwhitetrim@,&.> 0{c
hc=. ;:'GUID_Key Description Theorem Theorem_Alt Notes Attributions Links Rephrase'
'missing csv column(s)' assert hc e. hdr

wrcw=. {{ ((];._2)@tlf@((0{x)&wrapwords)&.> ((1{x) {"1 y) ,@,.&.> ' ') (<a:;1{x)} y }}

c=. (55,hdr i. <'Description') wrcw c
c=. (55,hdr i. <'Rephrase') wrcw c
c=. (30,hdr i. <'Theorem') wrcw c
c=. (30,hdr i. <'Theorem_Alt') wrcw c
c=. (30,hdr i. <'Notes') wrcw c
NB. c=. (30,hdr i. <'Attributions') wrcw c

NB. clip trailing link column blanks
c=. (rebtbcol&.> p {"1 c) (<a:;p)} c [ p=. hdr i. <'Links'

NB. remove any fully empty columns and blank cell rows
c=. rebrow&.> c #"1~ -.*./ 0 = #&> (,&.> }. c) -.&.> <' '
c=. c #~ +./"1 ] 0 < #&> c

NB. add item/total counts
c=. c ,.~ ('q</',(":<:#c),'>') 8!:0 i. #c
(<'Row_Total') (<0;0)} c
)

